    "cellpair_adds_information_beyond_family": true,
    "summary": "Family identity is a strong, reproducible organiser of interaction_strength_like_value: family labels explain 0.836 of record-level variance; shuffling family labels (keeping family sizes) collapses the between-family variance from 2.055 to about 0.718 (p<=0.002). The signal is not an artefact of unequal stage occupancy: the stage-adjusted family variance retains 85% of the raw between-family variance; nor of family size. Cell-pair identity adds only a small but detectable increment (8.0% of the residual after family), so families behave as near-blocks that differ between cell pairs only modestly."
  },
